WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.558 --> 00:00:04.331
- Hi everybody!

00:00:04.331 --> 00:00:06.851
Guess what day it is?

00:00:06.851 --> 00:00:09.884
- Monday.
- Monday!

00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:12.620
It's the day to get it done.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.570
I can tell you I need to go on a cleanse

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:19.180
because yeah, it was, the weekend.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.562
my daughter, it was her eighth birthday.

00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:23.730
(crowd cheers)

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.740
And she's actually here right now.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.580
My kids are here at work
with me, which is so amazing.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.100
They have the day off school
and we'll see how this goes.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.570
I'm so excited.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.760
I love you guys so much.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.970
My daughter turned eight this weekend.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.623
Eight! Eight.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.710
Eight.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:46.680
I mean, when people say
that it goes by so fast,

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.770
I feel like it's usually
people who are kind

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.080
of on the other side of it,

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.130
like looking in the rear view mirror

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:55.630
and they really know
how fast it does go by.

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:57.480
They're trying to warn you to be present,

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.500
but when you're in it,

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.060
the truth is it's more
like the Yiddish proverb

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.200
that the days are long
and the years are short.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.280
And when you're looking
back at the scrapbook

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.900
of your life it seems like an instant,

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.280
but I know right now being a parent is one

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.536
of the hardest things, the most rewarding,

00:01:14.536 --> 00:01:17.970
but we're all trying to be super heroes.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.180
And, you know, I had this amazing weekend

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.210
where I felt like finally for, you know

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.840
launching this show, I
had like the perfect kid

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.970
to life ratio and I was just all in

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:30.410
and I knew exactly what my
priorities were in life.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:31.770
And it just felt so good.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.453
Happy birthday, Olive.
(crowd cheers)

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.270
Cheers to being eight.

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:40.200
Cheers to me realizing I can't get away

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.560
with eating all that
leftover birthday cake

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.360
and the macaroni and cheese
and everything else that I had,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.140
I mean, just, I went on a food bender

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:52.240
and so yeah, I'm gonna be
cleansing this week a little bit.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.420
But listen, whether your motherhood

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.840
or as I love to call it other-hood,

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.350
I think one of the things
that's really being taught

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.770
to us right now in this wild
journey is to be present.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:07.970
And although time has stopped,
literally it's just stopped.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:10.933
We can't will that clock
to move any faster.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:15.780
We can try to be present together

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.420
and appreciate anything
and everything around us.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:22.590
In fact, Jasmine from Chicago,

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.440
I think you have your kids right?

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.280
- Yes. Yes, I have four.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.270
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:30.912
How are you juggling four?

00:02:30.912 --> 00:02:32.578
- I have no idea, but you know what,

00:02:32.578 --> 00:02:34.550
it's like you said, we're
enjoying the journey.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:36.830
It is an absolute blessing.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.540
- It really is.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:41.670
I had this like call with
the show this weekend

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:44.210
and we were just talking
about kids in this time

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.610
and we haven't lived like
this in a hundred years.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.090
All our societal norms
and agreements are gone.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:50.923
Work, school.
- Yep.

00:02:50.923 --> 00:02:52.010
- Everything's different.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:54.370
And I know how trying that is.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:56.530
And yet when I just let everything else go

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.730
and focus solely on my kids this weekend,

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.970
I knew what the purpose of my life was.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.750
And it was so wonderful.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.700
But you don't have to
be a parent for that.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.520
Like just finding something, someone,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.020
that gives you the meaning and the reason.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.670
- Yeah, yes.
- You have four.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.970
- Yes, yes. Four beautiful babies.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.530
I wouldn't have it any other way.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:18.090
Our life is complete. My heart is full.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.370
- Aw, cheers to you, Jasmine.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.373
Thank you for,

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.990
we can back each other
up on finding that love

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:30.733
and goodness in life and just
holding onto it for dear life!

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:34.150
- Yes!
- Thanks Jasmine,

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.530
cheers to you this morning.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:36.690
All right, we have a great show.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:37.750
We're gonna kick it off

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.870
with one of the classiest
women on the planet.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:44.510
The most extraordinary talent,
Julianne Moore is here.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:47.510
More and more and more,
look at her! Oh my goodness!

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.450
All right, and we're
gonna start with the news

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.810
as we like to serve it sunny side up,

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:53.822
it's time for Drew's News.

00:03:53.822 --> 00:03:55.840
(glass shattering)
(cat screeches)

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.343
Ma'am, I asked you a question!

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.993
It's Drew's News!

00:04:03.925 --> 00:04:07.120
Hi everybody! Walking to the news desk.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.390
All right, on Drew's News,

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.404
we find all of those good morsels

00:04:10.404 --> 00:04:12.370
that carry us throughout the day.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.220
And I love this section of the show

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.430
because I have so much
fun with the news crew,

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.200
the best people in the world.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.480
And we comb through for
these life affirming stories

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:24.690
of our country and the people in it.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:28.620
So we're actually shooting our
show here in New York City.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:31.460
And lately the restaurants
have been shifting

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.110
to outdoor dining and New
York City has felt more

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.940
like gay Paris and I love it.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.310
The New York Times reports
that the mayor has said

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:43.626
the outdoor dining theme
will continue year round.

00:04:43.626 --> 00:04:45.550
(crowd cheers)
I know!

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:49.040
I mean, it is pretty wild
when you live somewhere

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.070
and everything changes overnight

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.000
and the changes are positive.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.000
And then they're gonna stay.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.070
And New York has really felt
like a bustling European city

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:00.240
and I'm so excited for
the island of Manhattan

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.283
to have a renaissance.

00:05:03.338 --> 00:05:06.270
Aha, I'm going to have
a bagel after the show

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.280
and I'm gonna have it al fresco.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.062
(crowd cheers)
In other news,

00:05:10.062 --> 00:05:13.050
Vogue magazine has Lizzo on the cover

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.570
and I just love her so much.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:17.910
She looks exceptional on
this cover, like flawless.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:20.910
And in this article she
talks about body positivity

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.370
is not even enough.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.490
She would like it to be body normative.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.340
She wants to normalize her body

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:30.270
and she's a huge advocate
of the no filter beauty.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:33.680
And I am a big proponent of that as well.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.380
And she's doing it in her
way and we love her for that.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.000
And we cheer her on endlessly

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.460
because you have to be your
authentic self in this world.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:42.810
Sometimes that's all we have.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:46.470
So yay, Lizzo. We love you here so much.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.090
Everybody loves her.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:51.210
Okay, let's talk about some
more women who are crushing it.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:54.010
This story is everywhere right now.

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:57.960
Okay, this female surfer
rode the biggest wave

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:01.720
of the year and shattered
a Guinness World Record.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.860
I know. Wait until you see this.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:04.920
I mean, do we have footage?

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.280
She's a surfer from Brazil.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.600
Yeah. There you go.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.860
Named Maya Gabeira.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:14.200
And scientists say the wave
was basically 74 feet tall.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.800
That's two telephone
poles on top of each other

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:19.750
or five giraffes high.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.680
And what even makes this more inspiring is

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.560
that in 2013, Maya had an
accident, a near death crash

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:29.810
from a 50 foot wave,
not even nearly as big,

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:33.740
and it took her four years to
recover from it, but she did.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.060
And now she's back, okay?

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:39.534
She's getting back up
on that old wave horse,

00:06:39.534 --> 00:06:42.640
#TheOldWaveHorse, and
she's riding the biggest,

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.600
baddest waves in the world.

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.433
Now, wow.

00:06:45.433 --> 00:06:48.400
If that isn't a way to
show how you get back up,

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.330
I don't know what is.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.627
Thank you Maya for
showing us how it's done.

00:06:51.627 --> 00:06:53.370
(crowd cheers)

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:54.630
Okay, whoop, whoop!

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:57.063
It's time for a beauty junkie alert.

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:01.300
All right. I'm really
into this next story.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:04.860
And this goes out to all the
chins out there, all right.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.650
Are you sick and tired of mask-ne,

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.870
which is acne and what
comes from under your mask?

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:10.770
You heard me.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:13.420
Marie Claire has posted a
new soothing facial mask

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.213
that fits underneath your PPE.

00:07:16.232 --> 00:07:18.690
It's called the Soothe &amp;
Shield mask by Masque Bar

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:21.080
and it uses aloe and natural oils.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.680
I actually love even taking
a little aloe vera plant,

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:26.540
I'm from California,
so this is what we do.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.730
We go and hack a little thing off.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:31.290
And then you use the
natural aloe on your face.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:32.790
It's an amazing hack.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:35.290
And they sell them at
bodega's all around the city

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.470
and you can find them, you can plant them.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:40.460
Aloe vera is very easily
available where they have like

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.790
the herbs and stuff at your
local shops, it's there.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.330
And so you put this underneath your mask

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:49.660
and listen, we can't protect
ourselves enough, you know,

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:53.060
from COVID, and then this
can help you with your acne

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:53.893
and dry skin.

00:07:53.893 --> 00:07:56.961
And it's a winnie win win
for the chinny chin chin

00:07:56.961 --> 00:07:59.628
(upbeat music)

